From: Florent Revest <revestflo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Poll in passive mode only for reader/writer

Upstream-Status: Pending

Tags only talk in passive communication mode, active mode is for
NFC-DEP peers. Asking for ActivePollA/F in reader/writer mode made the
NXP SN220U (Pixel Watch 2) reject RF_DISCOVER_CMD with STATUS_REJECTED,
so discovery never started. Keep active polling for peer mode only.
---
 src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c b/src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c
index ac213ff..d469c89 100644
--- a/src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c
+++ b/src/nci_transition_idle_to_discovery.c
@@ -298,9 +298,14 @@ nci_transition_idle_to_discovery_discover(
      */
 
     if (sm->op_mode & NFC_OP_MODE_RW) {
-        techs |= NCI_TECH_A_POLL |
+        /*
+         * Tags only talk in passive communication mode. Active mode
+         * (NFC-DEP) is only needed for peer-to-peer, and some NFCCs
+         * (NXP SN220) reject RF_DISCOVER_CMD that asks for it.
+         */
+        techs |= NCI_TECH_A_POLL_PASSIVE |
             NCI_TECH_B_POLL |
-            NCI_TECH_F_POLL |
+            NCI_TECH_F_POLL_PASSIVE |
             NCI_TECH_V_POLL;
     }
 
